Because $3$ is a prime number, any power of three (including $3^{19}$) can only be evenly divided by smaller powers of three. Therefore, we can simply check if `n` is greater than $0$ and if $3^{19}$ is perfectly divisible by `n`.

```java
class Solution {
    public boolean isPowerOfThree(int n) {
        // The maximum power of 3 that fits in a 32-bit signed integer is 3^19 = 1162261467
        return n > 0 && 1162261467 % n == 0;
    }
}
```

